{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_vrtx_01J5Egv369SV869xsJRmH5zt","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-4-7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait, I used `loopsDir` and `skillsDir` but then also set `loops_dir` to `\"<loops_dir>\"` and `skills_dir` to `\"<skills_dir>\"`. That means `loopsDir` and `skillsDir` are being computed but only `loopsDir` is passed to `LoadLoopsContext`. That `_ = skillsDir` is ugly. Let me rethink this.\n\nActually, in the dry-run:\n- `loops_dir` → `\"<loops_dir>\"` (placeholder, not real path)\n- `skills_dir` → `\"<skills_dir>\"` (placeholder, not real path) \n- `loops_context` → `LoadLoopsContext(loopsDir)` (real content based on actual loopsDir)\n\nBut `loopsDir` is constructed from `rickDir` and the \"loops\" subdirectory, which may not exist—though `LoadLoopsContext` handles that gracefully. Since I'm only using the placeholder string for `skills_dir` in the dry-run, I don't actually need to compute `skillsDir` at all. I can simplify this.","signature":""}],"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9798c368-b480-4d08-a4e0-bb572b54b4d9","uuid":"5f9b820a-1463-4790-b6f0-2bb03f897f92"}
